#  PURPOSE: ASSOCIATED_WITH is the universal base relation for every edge in
#  the KG -- confirmed by the project owner 2026-09-14 -- with a more
#  specific relation type (TARGET, TREAT, CAUSES, etc.) optionally layered
#  on top where the source data supports it. This rule applies to every
#  graph regardless of skg-source, not just today's two offenders.
#
#  Biovista already follows this (every edge is ASSOCIATED_WITH,
#  exclusively). Radboud and Demokritos do not: many of their
#  specific-relation graphs carry no accompanying ASSOCIATED_WITH base tag.
#  Confirmed 2026-09-14 by direct read-only query against the live triple
#  store (not inferred from the offline .large dumps):
#    - Radboud: 48,471 total graphs; 44,909 have ASSOCIATED_WITH
#      (Disease-Gene + Phenotype-Gene, both hardcode it); 3,562 do not
#      (3,153 TARGET / Drug-Gene + 409 TREAT / Drug-Disease+Drug-Phenotype).
#    - Demokritos: 10,269 total graphs; only 487 have ASSOCIATED_WITH;
#      9,782 do not.
#  Total currently missing the base tag: 13,344 graphs.
#
#  This is an INSERT-only patch: it ADDS a second simp:source-relation
#  triple to each affected graph, alongside its existing specific relation
#  (TARGET, TREAT, CAUSES, ...) -- it does not remove or replace anything.
#  Written partner-agnostic (no skg-source filter) so it correctly applies
#  the same universal rule to any future partner's data too, not just
#  today's known gap.
#
#  VERIFY BEFORE (read-only, no auth needed):
#    PREFIX simp: <urn:simpathic:>
#    SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?g) AS ?n) WHERE {
#      GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:skg-source ?source . }
#      MINUS {
#        GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:source-relation "ASSOCIATED_WITH" . }
#      }
#    }
#  Expected result before this patch: 13344
#
#  VERIFY AFTER: re-run the same SELECT above. Expected result: 0.

PREFIX simp: <urn:simpathic:>

INSERT {
  GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:source-relation "ASSOCIATED_WITH" . }
}
WHERE {
  GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:skg-source ?source . }
  MINUS {
    GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:source-relation "ASSOCIATED_WITH" . }
  }
}
